{"name":"Meristem","hex":"#aae1ce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meristem","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant tissue composed of totipotent cells that allows plant growth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meristem"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meristem","blocks":[{"text":"In cell biology, the meristem is a structure composed of specialized tissue found in plants, consisting of stem cells, known as meristematic cells, which are undifferentiated cells capable of continuous cellular division. These meristematic cells play a fundamental role in plant growth, regeneration, and acclimatization, as they serve as the source of all differentiated plant tissues and organs. They contribute to the formation of structures such as fruits, leaves, and seeds, as well as supportive tissues like stems and roots."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/M%C3%A9rist%C3%A8me_couches.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meristem","wikidata":"Q207604"},{"title":"Meristem (school)","blocks":[{"text":"Meristem is a non-profit school for young adults with autism spectrum and other neurodevelopmental disorders in Fair Oaks, California."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meristem_(school)","wikidata":"Q124381943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/M%C3%A9rist%C3%A8me_coupe_zones_chiffres.png/500px-M%C3%A9rist%C3%A8me_coupe_zones_chiffres.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/M%C3%A9rist%C3%A8me_coupe_zones_chiffres.png/500px-M%C3%A9rist%C3%A8me_coupe_zones_chiffres.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Organisation of an apical meristem (growing tip)Central zonePeripheral zoneMedullary (i.e. central) meristemMedullary tissue","link":"htt